# Block: children stacked from top to bottom, each with the full width unless it declares its own.
Document (dev.stxt.pdf):
	Language: en
	Title: Block · Stacking
	Page:
		Paper: A4
		Margin: 20mm
	Styles:
		For style: piece
			Box:
				Padding: 6 8
				Margin: 0 0 6 0
				Background: tint
	Section:
		Text: Block
			Style: topic
		Heading 1:
			Text: Stacking
		Paragraph: A `Block` places its children one below another, in document order. A child without `Width` takes the full width of the block, and one with `Width` and `Margin: 0 auto` is centered.
			Style: intro
		Text: Block with three children
			Style: label
		Block:
			Style: sample
			Text: First child: the full width.
				Style: piece
			Text: Second child: Width 50%, at the left.
				Style: piece
				Box:
					Width: 50%
			Text: Third child: Width 50%, Margin 0 auto.
				Style: piece
				Box:
					Width: 50%
					Margin: 0 auto 6 auto
		Text: Height: 120 (the block measures what it declares)
			Style: label
		Block:
			Style: sample
			Box:
				Height: 120
			Text: One child in a block of a fixed height.
				Style: piece
		Text: Typography: Italic: true, Color: accent (inherited by the children)
			Style: label
		Block:
			Style: sample
			Typography:
				Italic: true
				Color: accent
			Text: Both texts inherit the typography of their block.
			Text: Only Typography is inherited: Box and Break are not.
